  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: The top-5 experiments all use multiprofile, with config_039 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) leading at 0.7250 acc. scvi_n200 is clearly the best RNA encoder (0.72 vs 0.52 for scgpt), imagenet_vit_l edges out resnet50 on accuracy, transformer beats avgpool, and weighted slightly beats concat. However, the profile setting (multiprofile vs singleprofile) is a major architectural dimension that has been completely untested. Question: config_032 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + singleprofile + weighted) is a clean ablation of config_039 with only the profile setting changed, directly testing whether the multiprofile + transformer aggregation pipeline is essential or whether a simpler single-profile fusion can match or exceed it. Why this is the best next experiment: With 4 experiments remaining, resolving whether singleprofile is competitive is critical—if it is, it opens a new search axis; if not, we can confidently commit remaining budget to refining the multiprofile + transformer + weighted pipeline. It retains all the individually validated best components (top RNA encoder, top image encoder, best fusion) while probing the single largest untested design choice."
}

